  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\cauchy.rational.sequence]\nDeclares: A ::= a(n_) ::= q_\nspecifies:\n. n_ is \\natural\n. q_ is \\rational\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: epsilon is \\rational\n  where: \\rational.zero \\:rational.less?:/ epsilon\n  then:\n  . exists: N is \\natural\n    suchThat:\n    . forAll: m, n is \\natural\n      where:\n      . N \\:natural.leq?:/ m\n      . N \\:natural.leq?:/ n\n      then: \\rational.abs(a(m) \\.rational.-./ a(n)) \\:rational.less?:/ epsilon\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Cauchy rational sequence\"\n. description: \"A rational sequence is Cauchy when its terms eventually lie\n                within every positive rational distance of one another.\"\nId: \"db1721ae-e0d4-4421-abc3-a586c0865ea5\"",
